# Marker-directed panel composition

## Current general rule

Public parent `7491f3cf`; canonical rule ID `ee_7491f3cf`. The authored general
Racket reference reproduces all four original demonstrations and the provided
test answer. It loads no fixtures or original grids.

Parse four equal panels in row-major order inside a uniform separator frame.
The first panel contains a long divider and a separate singleton hint of the
same color. Eight-connectivity identifies the divider; four-connectivity of its
complement identifies the hint's side, including bent dividers. The second
panel supplies the marked side and the third panel supplies the other side.
On divider cells, overlay the second panel's nonbackground first, falling back
to the third. Only the final destination panel is changed.

`side_assignment=marker_first` is the exact canonical reference. Alternative
`marker_second` swaps which source supplies the indicated and complementary
regions, while retaining the same boundary overlay policy and geometric parsing.
The alternative therefore changes source selection across whole regions rather
than dropping the input-dependent reasoning step.

## Admitted grammar and sampling

Four equal square panels, blank destination, distinct frame/background/ink/source
colors, one 8-connected divider and one nonadjacent singleton hint, exactly two
4-connected complementary regions. Ordinary parents are horizontal 5×5 panels;
the authored grammar also supports vertical and 2×2 tables, panel sizes 5–13,
straight/diagonal/bent/zigzag dividers, rotations/reflections, and thick exterior
padding. These extensions are explicit authoring choices, not uniquely inferred
from the finite original examples. Arbitrary junctions, multiple hints, more than
two regions and nonblank destinations are outside the admitted grammar.

Support: independently requested 2–6 demonstrations and 1–4 query prefixes;
all four distinct queries are retained privately, and inputs are matched across
settings. A separate presentation seed shuffles the complete query bank before
selecting a turn. Model-visible data contains only demonstration input/output
and the current query input. The 30×30 stress case has four 13×13 panels and a
two-bend divider; it tests substantial content and large region topology, not
just empty padding.

## Teaching repairs

The initial two-demo sampler admitted two concrete wrong rules:

- Seed 1: always give the denser source the marked side.
- Seed 17: replace a bent divider with a straight half-plane through its endpoints.

Both were reproduced by independent executable Racket rivals on the two fitting
demonstrations and a disagreeing query (twelve protected evaluations), retained
in `tests/retained_shortcuts.json`. Tiny L-shaped dividers can be geometrically
indistinguishable from their endpoint chord on a coarse grid, or lack colored
source evidence on the differing cells. The second demonstration now uses a
larger centered bend and explicitly contrasting source pixels at a cell where
the actual region and endpoint half-plane differ. The first two demonstrations
also reverse source area and palette ordering, preventing those choices from
masquerading as panel-position semantics. Boundary cases include both conflicts
and fallback, and hint pixels expose treating the singleton as divider geometry.

Final suite: 43 tests passed. Source-bound authoring preflight checks all five
original labels, ordinary generator calls, and both settings on seeds 17/43 with
two demonstrations and four queries. Final finite audit: 64 seeds × two settings
× every demo count 2–6 = 640 nested lesson views / 5,120 reused pair exposures;
zero query-changing survivors among 25 executable Python rivals. A separate
maximum-demo check uses protected Racket. Sixteen hashed single-query exports
pass private-field, future-query and short-prefix invariance checks.

## Sequential dependency and evidence

A extracts the divider and performs the hint-directed four-neighbor flood. Its
intermediate is the exact selected-region mask. B uses that mask to choose a
source at each non-divider cell. Replacing it with the empty set changes 57 cells
on the source-bound 30×30 marker_second witness; construction and a new protected
runtime replay both pass. This tests causal dependence of final labels, not a
claim that finite traces establish universal algorithmic depth.

Reproduce from the packet root using new output directories:

```
python3 review.py run python3 -m pytest generators/public_eval_7491f3cf/tests -q
python3 review.py run python3 -m arcpuzzles.review_public_creation preflight public_eval_7491f3cf --root . --out ../checks/public_eval_7491f3cf/NEW-preflight
python3 review.py run python3 generators/public_eval_7491f3cf/workspace/parametric/audit.py --preflight ../checks/public_eval_7491f3cf/NEW-preflight/preflight.json --out ../checks/public_eval_7491f3cf/NEW-audit --seeds 64
```

Current evidence: `checks/public_eval_7491f3cf/preflight/` and
`checks/public_eval_7491f3cf/audit/`. Earlier failing tests are development evidence,
not final-source failures. Reviewer-ready only. Owner registration, exact-source
native qualification/acceptance, training admission and learning-gain measurement
remain separate. Finite tested policies do not establish universal identifiability.
